IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clpa-dates`

-- Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993 (Victoria) -- the whole Act, as the CLAIMANT meets it.
--
-- SEAT: the person who brings a claim (for example for an injury suffered in another State, a Territory or New Zealand)
-- before a court or an arbitrator in Victoria, where the law of that other place governs the claim. "Is this time limit
-- a limitation law?", "Does the Act reach my proceeding?", "Whose limitation law will the court apply to my claim?",
-- "How will the court use a power to extend time under that law?", "Am I in time, and by when must I start?". The
-- person who answers the claim meets the same rules from the other side (NOTES.md, Seat); the court, the arbitrator and
-- the courts of the other place get no seat.
--
-- The Act is six sections. It is a gate in front of a limitation period: it decides WHOSE limitation law applies, not
-- what that law says. The other place's limitation law is not deposited; its period, the day it runs from and whether
-- it gives a discretion to extend are asked as facts. Which place's substantive law governs the claim is decided by the
-- court under the rules of choice of law, which are outside this Act: it is asked as a fact. Whether a court extends
-- time is the court's judgment: it is asked, never decided.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list). The limitation period is a
-- DEONTIC rule run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Choice of Law
-- (Limitation Periods) Act 1993, Act No. 100/1993, Version No. 003 (16 August 2012), not the authorised version.
-- (c) State of Victoria; published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may
-- be reproduced except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October
-- 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993: the claimant's questions`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `The facts the Act turns on`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 3 "court includes arbitrator". s 5 and s 6 speak of "a court of this State" and "a court of the State": with the
-- definition, a Victorian court or an arbitrator in Victoria (fork F1).
DECLARE `Where my claim is heard` IS ONE OF
    `a court of Victoria`
    `an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Victoria`
    `a court or an arbitrator outside Victoria`

-- s 5, s 6 "another place being another State, a Territory or New Zealand". "State" and "Territory" are not defined in
-- the Act (borrowed: asked by choice; fork F2). Victoria itself is not "another place".
DECLARE `Place` IS ONE OF
    `Victoria`
    `another Australian State (New South Wales, Queensland, South Australia, Tasmania or Western Australia)`
    `an Australian Territory (for example the Australian Capital Territory or the Northern Territory)`
    `New Zealand`
    `a country other than Australia or New Zealand`

GIVEN `the place` IS A `Place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 5, 6 -- another place being another State, a Territory or New Zealand` `the place` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `another Australian State (New South Wales, Queensland, South Australia, Tasmania or Western Australia)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Australian Territory (for example the Australian Capital Territory or the Northern Territory)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `New Zealand` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 3, 5, 6 -- a court of this State` `where heard` IF
    CONSIDER `where heard`
    WHEN `a court of Victoria` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Victoria` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 3 -- what a limitation law is`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 3 "limitation law means a law that provides for the limitation of any liability or the barring of a right of action
-- in respect of a claim by reference to the time when a proceeding on, or the arbitration of, the claim is commenced."
-- A "means" definition: JUST TRUE when both limbs hold, JUST FALSE otherwise.
GIVEN `it limits a liability or bars a right of action on a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so by the time a proceeding or arbitration is started` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- a limitation law` `it limits a liability or bars a right of action on a claim` `it does so by the time a proceeding or arbitration is started` MEANS
    IF `it limits a liability or bars a right of action on a claim` AND `it does so by the time a proceeding or arbitration is started`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@export Is the time limit I face a "limitation law" under the Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993 (Victoria) s 3? A limitation law is a law that limits a liability, or bars a right of action, on a claim by reference to the time when a proceeding on the claim (or its arbitration) is started. A time limit for something else, such as giving notice of a claim or lodging a claim form, is not one unless it works by the time a proceeding is started.
GIVEN `limits or bars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law limits a liability, or bars a right of action, on your claim (for example it says no action may be brought, or the liability ends)
      `by the time proceedings start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it does so by reference to the time when a court proceeding, or an arbitration, on your claim is started (for example "an action may not be brought after 3 years"), rather than by reference to some other step
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this a limitation law` MEANS
    `s 3 -- a limitation law` `limits or bars` `by the time proceedings start`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 2, 4 -- whether the Act reaches my proceeding`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 2 "This Act comes into operation on the day on which it receives the Royal Assent." The endnotes: assented to on
-- 23 November 1993 and came into operation on 23 November 1993. s 4 has no commencement of its own, so "the
-- commencement of this section" is that day.
`the day this Act came into operation` MEANS `the calendar date` 23 11 1993

-- s 4 "This Act extends to a cause of action that arose before the commencement of this section but does not apply to
-- proceedings instituted before the commencement of this section." A flat negative: JUST FALSE kind for a proceeding
-- instituted before 23 November 1993. One instituted on 23 November 1993 is not instituted "before" it (fork F3).
DECLARE `Does the Act reach my proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose on or after 23 November 1993`
    `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose before 23 November 1993, and s 4 extends the Act to it`
    `no: the Act does not apply to a proceeding instituted before 23 November 1993 (s 4)`

GIVEN `the day instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 -- instituted before the commencement` `the day instituted` IF
    `the day` `the day instituted` `is before` `the day this Act came into operation`

GIVEN `the day the cause arose` IS A DATE, `the day instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Does the Act reach my proceeding`
`ss 2, 4 -- the Act reaches my proceeding` `the day the cause arose` `the day instituted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 4 -- instituted before the commencement` `the day instituted`
        THEN `no: the Act does not apply to a proceeding instituted before 23 November 1993 (s 4)`
        IF `the day` `the day the cause arose` `is before` `the day this Act came into operation`
        THEN `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose before 23 November 1993, and s 4 extends the Act to it`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose on or after 23 November 1993`

@export Does the Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993 (Victoria) reach my proceeding (ss 2, 4)? The Act came into operation on 23 November 1993. It reaches a cause of action that arose before that day, but it does not apply to a proceeding instituted before that day.
GIVEN `day cause arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action arose (for example the day you were injured), as an ISO date such as 2025-03-14
      `day instituted` IS A DATE @desc The day your court proceeding was, or will be, started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date
GIVETH A `Does the Act reach my proceeding`
`Does the Act reach my proceeding` MEANS
    `ss 2, 4 -- the Act reaches my proceeding` `day cause arose` `day instituted`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 5 -- whose limitation law the court applies`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 5 "If the substantive law of another place being another State, a Territory or New Zealand, is to govern a claim
-- before a court of this State, a limitation law of that place is to be regarded as part of that substantive law and
-- applied accordingly by the court."
-- "If": when a limb fails, s 5 does not apply (JUST FALSE kind). Which limitation law then applies is outside the Act.
-- Which place's substantive law governs the claim is the court's choice-of-law decision: asked.
DECLARE `The limitation law the court applies` IS ONE OF
    `that place's limitation law, as part of the substantive law that governs my claim (s 5)`
    `s 5 does not apply: my claim is not before a court or an arbitrator of Victoria`
    `s 5 does not apply: my proceeding was instituted before 23 November 1993 (s 4)`
    `s 5 does not apply: Victorian law governs my claim; Victoria's own limitation law is outside this Act`
    `s 5 does not apply: the law of a country other than New Zealand governs my claim; which limitation law applies is outside this Act`

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `the day instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The limitation law the court applies`
`s 5 -- the limitation law the court applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day instituted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`ss 3, 5, 6 -- a court of this State` `where heard`)
        THEN `s 5 does not apply: my claim is not before a court or an arbitrator of Victoria`
        IF `s 4 -- instituted before the commencement` `the day instituted`
        THEN `s 5 does not apply: my proceeding was instituted before 23 November 1993 (s 4)`
        IF `ss 5, 6 -- another place being another State, a Territory or New Zealand` `the governing place`
        THEN `that place's limitation law, as part of the substantive law that governs my claim (s 5)`
        IF `the governing place` EQUALS `Victoria`
        THEN `s 5 does not apply: Victorian law governs my claim; Victoria's own limitation law is outside this Act`
        OTHERWISE `s 5 does not apply: the law of a country other than New Zealand governs my claim; which limitation law applies is outside this Act`

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `the day instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5 applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day instituted` IF
    `s 5 -- the limitation law the court applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day instituted` EQUALS `that place's limitation law, as part of the substantive law that governs my claim (s 5)`

@export Whose limitation law will the Victorian court (or arbitrator) apply to my claim (Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993 (Victoria) s 5)? If the substantive law of another State, a Territory or New Zealand governs your claim before a court or arbitrator in Victoria, that place's limitation law counts as part of its substantive law and the court applies it, not Victoria's. Which place's law governs your claim is for the court under the rules of choice of law, which this Act does not decide.
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard` @desc Where your claim is heard: a court of Victoria; an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Victoria; or a court or an arbitrator outside Victoria
      `governing place` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose substantive law governs your claim, as the court decides under the rules of choice of law: Victoria; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `day instituted` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding was, or will be, started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date
GIVETH A `The limitation law the court applies`
`Whose limitation law applies to my claim` MEANS
    `s 5 -- the limitation law the court applies` `where heard` `governing place` `day instituted`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 6 -- how a discretion under that limitation law is used`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 6 "If a court of the State exercises a discretion conferred under a limitation law of a place being another State, a
-- Territory or New Zealand that discretion, as far as practicable, is to be exercised in the manner in which it is
-- exercised in comparable cases by the courts of that place."
-- "If": when a limb fails, s 6 does not apply (JUST FALSE kind). Whether that law confers a discretion is that law's
-- (asked); how it comes out is the court's judgment (never decided).
DECLARE `How the discretion is exercised` IS ONE OF
    `as far as practicable, in the manner in which the courts of that place exercise it in comparable cases (s 6)`
    `s 6 does not apply: the discretion is not exercised by a court or an arbitrator of Victoria`
    `s 6 does not apply: my proceeding was instituted before 23 November 1993 (s 4)`
    `s 6 does not apply: the limitation law is not one of another State, a Territory or New Zealand`
    `s 6 does not apply: that place's limitation law confers no discretion in my case`

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the place of the limitation law` IS A `Place`
      `that law confers a discretion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `How the discretion is exercised`
`s 6 -- how the discretion is exercised` `where heard` `the place of the limitation law` `that law confers a discretion` `the day instituted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`ss 3, 5, 6 -- a court of this State` `where heard`)
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: the discretion is not exercised by a court or an arbitrator of Victoria`
        IF `s 4 -- instituted before the commencement` `the day instituted`
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: my proceeding was instituted before 23 November 1993 (s 4)`
        IF NOT (`ss 5, 6 -- another place being another State, a Territory or New Zealand` `the place of the limitation law`)
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: the limitation law is not one of another State, a Territory or New Zealand`
        IF NOT (`that law confers a discretion`)
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: that place's limitation law confers no discretion in my case`
        OTHERWISE `as far as practicable, in the manner in which the courts of that place exercise it in comparable cases (s 6)`

@export If the limitation law of another State, a Territory or New Zealand gives the court a discretion (for example to extend the time for starting my claim), how will the Victorian court use it (Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993 (Victoria) s 6)? As far as practicable, the court exercises it in the way the courts of that place exercise it in comparable cases. Whether it will be exercised in your favour is for the court; this question does not decide it.
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard` @desc Where your claim is heard: a court of Victoria; an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Victoria; or a court or an arbitrator outside Victoria
      `place of the limitation law` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose limitation law gives the discretion: Victoria; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `confers a discretion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that place's limitation law gives the court a discretion in your case (for example a power to extend the limitation period)
      `day instituted` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding was, or will be, started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date
GIVETH A `How the discretion is exercised`
`How will the court use a discretion under that law` MEANS
    `s 6 -- how the discretion is exercised` `where heard` `place of the limitation law` `confers a discretion` `day instituted`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 5, 6 -- am I in time under that place's limitation law`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- What s 5 means for the claimant: the period of the other place's limitation law is the one to meet. The period, the
-- day it runs from and any extension are that law's and that court's (asked). The last day is the same day of the month
-- the period's years and months after the day it runs from (fork F5; F6 for a day the month lacks); starting on the
-- last day is in time, the day after is not.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `I`
DECLARE `Act done` IS ONE OF `start my proceeding or arbitration`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 5 -- start within that place's limitation period` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `start my proceeding or arbitration`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "the proceeding was not started within the limitation period of the place whose law governs the claim, which s 5 makes the Victorian court apply"

-- The helper that runs the rule over what happened (as in the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria),
-- Victims of Crime and County Court encodings). On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not
-- BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
      `the time it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `started in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was done`), (EVENT `I` `start my proceeding or arbitration` `the time it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Started on or before the last day? A proceeding started before the period begins to run is in time (fork F7).
GIVEN `the day the period runs from` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE, `the day instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `started by the last day` `the day the period runs from` `the last day` `the day instituted` IF
    IF `the day` `the day instituted` `is before` `the day the period runs from`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `started in time under` (`s 5 -- start within that place's limitation period` (`the days from` `the day the period runs from` `to` `the last day`)) `at` (`the days from` `the day the period runs from` `to` `the day instituted`)

DECLARE `Am I in time` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 5 does not make another place's limitation law apply to my claim (ask whose limitation law applies)`
    `yes, in time: I start within that place's limitation period, which the court applies (s 5)`
    `no, out of time under that place's limitation period (s 5), unless the court extends the time under a discretion that law gives, exercised as that place's courts would (s 6)`
    `yes, in time: the court has extended the time under that place's limitation law (s 6), and I start by the extended day`
    `no, out of time even as the court extended it under that place's limitation law (s 6)`

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `the years` IS A NUMBER
      `the months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the period runs from` IS A DATE
      `the time was extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
      `the day instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Am I in time`
`ss 5, 6 -- am I in time` `where heard` `the governing place` `the years` `the months` `the day the period runs from` `the time was extended` `the extended last day` `the day instituted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 5 applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day instituted`)
        THEN `not covered: s 5 does not make another place's limitation law apply to my claim (ask whose limitation law applies)`
        IF `the time was extended`
        THEN IF `started by the last day` `the day the period runs from` `the extended last day` `the day instituted`
             THEN `yes, in time: the court has extended the time under that place's limitation law (s 6), and I start by the extended day`
             ELSE `no, out of time even as the court extended it under that place's limitation law (s 6)`
        IF `started by the last day` `the day the period runs from` (`the date` `the years` `years and` `the months` `months after` `the day the period runs from`) `the day instituted`
        THEN `yes, in time: I start within that place's limitation period, which the court applies (s 5)`
        OTHERWISE `no, out of time under that place's limitation period (s 5), unless the court extends the time under a discretion that law gives, exercised as that place's courts would (s 6)`

@export Am I in time to start my claim in Victoria when another State's, a Territory's or New Zealand's law governs it (Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993 (Victoria) ss 5, 6)? The court applies that place's limitation period, not Victoria's. Give the period that place's law sets for your claim and the day it runs from (both from that place's law, which this question does not hold), and say whether the court has extended the time under that law. Whether it will extend is for the court.
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard` @desc Where your claim is heard: a court of Victoria; an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Victoria; or a court or an arbitrator outside Victoria
      `governing place` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose substantive law governs your claim, as the court decides under the rules of choice of law: Victoria; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `period years` IS A NUMBER @desc The whole years in the limitation period that place's law sets for your claim (for example 3); 0 if the period is in months only
      `period months` IS A NUMBER @desc Any further whole months in that period (for example 0, or 6); 0 if none
      `period runs from` IS A DATE @desc The day that place's law says the period runs from (for example the day your cause of action arose, or the day you discovered it), as an ISO date
      `time extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has extended the time for starting your claim under a discretion in that place's limitation law
      `extended last day` IS A DATE @desc If the time was extended, the last day the court allowed, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day instituted` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding was, or will be, started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date
GIVETH A `Am I in time`
`Am I in time under that place's limitation law` MEANS
    `ss 5, 6 -- am I in time` `where heard` `governing place` `period years` `period months` `period runs from` `time extended` `extended last day` `day instituted`

-- The last day to start: the extended day if the court extended the time, otherwise the period counted from the day it
-- runs from. NOTHING where s 5 does not make another place's limitation law apply (the Act then sets no day).
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `the years` IS A NUMBER
      `the months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the period runs from` IS A DATE
      `the time was extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
      `the day instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 5, 6 -- the last day to start` `where heard` `the governing place` `the years` `the months` `the day the period runs from` `the time was extended` `the extended last day` `the day instituted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 5 applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day instituted`)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the time was extended`
        THEN JUST `the extended last day`
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the date` `the years` `years and` `the months` `months after` `the day the period runs from`)

@export By when must I start my claim in Victoria when another State's, a Territory's or New Zealand's law governs it (Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993 (Victoria) ss 5, 6)? The last day of that place's limitation period, counted from the day that law says it runs from; or the later day the court allowed, if it extended the time under that law. No answer if s 5 does not apply to your claim.
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard` @desc Where your claim is heard: a court of Victoria; an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Victoria; or a court or an arbitrator outside Victoria
      `governing place` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose substantive law governs your claim, as the court decides under the rules of choice of law: Victoria; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `period years` IS A NUMBER @desc The whole years in the limitation period that place's law sets for your claim (for example 3); 0 if the period is in months only
      `period months` IS A NUMBER @desc Any further whole months in that period (for example 0, or 6); 0 if none
      `period runs from` IS A DATE @desc The day that place's law says the period runs from (for example the day your cause of action arose, or the day you discovered it), as an ISO date
      `time extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has extended the time for starting your claim under a discretion in that place's limitation law
      `extended last day` IS A DATE @desc If the time was extended, the last day the court allowed, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day instituted` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding will be started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date; it decides only whether s 4 lets the Act apply (before 23 November 1993 it does not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I start my claim` MEANS
    `ss 5, 6 -- the last day to start` `where heard` `governing place` `period years` `period months` `period runs from` `time extended` `extended last day` `day instituted`
